Overlay patch 0019 (rev4): harden Metal UploadTexture — clamp + null-guard
+ exact byte accounting + deferred mip-chain generation.
rev1 (HD-pack pause crash): Metal ABORTS the process (driver-side
descriptor validation, active in release builds) when a texture dimension
exceeds the GPU limit — 8192 on the simulator, 16384 on A-series phones.
No pack texture is really that big (OoT Reloaded HD maxes at 2560, 4K at
8192): Interpreter::ImportTextureRaw's OOB-load fallback flattens a load
request larger than the HD resource into a SINGLE LINE, so a 64 KB
resource becomes a 16384x1 upload (sim abort) and the 4K pack's Kaleido
strip is 65536x1 (device abort). Clamp to the device max; the flattened
data past the clamp is zero-fill/garbage by construction. bytes_per_row
stays the SOURCE stride so a clamped region reads row-correct sub-rects.
rev2 (4K long-session pause crash): (a) newTexture returns nil under
memory pressure and the unchecked replaceRegion dereferenced it — now
skips with an error log instead of crashing; (b) exact GPU texture byte
accounting (add on create, subtract on the dim-mismatch release) feeding
GetTextureBytes/the 0020 byte-budget cache eviction.
rev3 (4K GPU overload): HD/4K replacement textures uploaded with a single
mip level — minified sampling of 2048px+ textures is a memory-bandwidth
catastrophe (device gpu_ms hit 31 ms/frame in vista scenes; 3.8 ms with
mips). Large textures get a full mip chain, generated on the GPU.
rev4 (Hyrule Field freeze, Vision Pro 2026-07-15): rev3 committed a fresh
command buffer per upload MID-FRAME. StartDrawToFramebuffer enqueue()s
the frame's command buffer before the display list runs, and Metal
executes a queue's command buffers strictly in enqueue order — so every
per-upload buffer queued behind an enqueued-but-UNCOMMITTED buffer.
Past ~63 uploads in one frame (Hyrule Field cold-cache burst, 4K pack)
commandBuffer() blocks forever waiting for a slot that can only free
when the frame buffer commits — which the blocked main thread will never
do. Scenes with smaller bursts (title, Kokiri) drained each frame and
masked it. Fix: zero mid-frame command buffers — uploads push the texture
(retained; 0020's eviction can release it first) onto a pending list, and
EndFrame encodes ONE generateMipmaps blit pass on the frame's own command
buffer after its render encoding ends. Mips become valid next frame; the
one frame that samples fresh uploads pre-mips is a load transition.
Ledger sites are mip-aware (a full chain is +1/3 of the base level).

